---
---`DELETE /v2/aliases/{aliasId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.aliases.DeleteAliasRequest
---@return vercel.aliases.DeleteAliasResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_alias(input) end

---Get an Alias
---
---Retrieves an Alias for the given host name or alias ID.
---
---`GET /v4/aliases/{idOrAlias}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.aliases.GetAliasRequest
---@return vercel.aliases.GetAliasResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_alias(input) end

---List aliases
---
---Retrieves a list of aliases for the authenticated User or Team. When `domain` is provided, only aliases for that domain will be returned. When `projectId` is provided, it will only return the given project aliases.
---
---`GET /v4/aliases`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input? vercel.aliases.ListAliasesRequest
---@return vercel.aliases.ListAliasesResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_aliases(input) end

---List Deployment Aliases
---
---Retrieves all Aliases for the Deployment with the given ID. The authenticated user or team must own the deployment.
---
---`GET /v2/deployments/{id}/aliases`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input vercel.aliases.ListDeploymentAliasesRequest
---@return vercel.aliases.ListDeploymentAliasesResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_deployment_aliases(input) end

---Update the protection bypass for a URL
---
---Update the protection bypass for the alias or deployment URL (used for user access & comment access for deployments). Used as shareable links and user scoped access for Vercel Authentication and also to allow external (logged in) people to comment on previews for Preview Comments (next-live-mode).
---
---`PATCH /aliases/{id}/protection-bypass`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input vercel.aliases.PatchUrlProtectionBypassRequest
---@return vercel.aliases.PatchUrlProtectionBypassResponseBodyMap? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:patch_url_protection_bypass(input) end

